It's from a color Sunday strip.

An alien ship showed up in Earth orbit, lowered a tube,
and sucked up all the water from the oceans, to be
transported back to its home galaxy.  It then began
to suck up all the air, causing a public outcry among
the humans.  The aliens responded to the effect that
they were sorry to learn that taking our atmosphere
would result in our deaths, but they were unwilling to
stop, because...  they didn't want to lose their jobs
(which, presumably, consist of gathering water and
air from planets in various other galaxies).

The comic tells the story better than I have done,
in verse, and of course with illustrations.

In the last panel, it's revealed that this is a story
Calvin is writing.  Hobbes isn't sure it's quite
far-fetched enough for sci-fi audiences.


